{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.717971Z","id":"dbb3f8a4af960c891c35f4acbff42152dafadbc6ce81d1822beda2f284a3d1df","body":{"detail":"After DELETE /api/artifacts/<A>/db-grants/<B>, the hub (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs reader_routes, the per-event may_read check) stops sending B's doc events on docs:<B>?reader=<A>, so web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts onStream (line 164) never schedules a refetch and the error callback is not called. web/e2e/db-artifact.spec.ts:84-85 pins exactly that: after the revoke, #runs keeps '5,7' and #err stays ''. The subscription, its stream topic and the page's last snapshot stay until a ready/resync triggers a refused refetch. The same text is in apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/clax-extensions.d.ts:80-85, which the app's agent reads, and cross-read.ts:19-20 and record 44415b80 describe the ending as if it followed the revoke. Live updates do stop at once, so no new data of B reaches the page.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:a8c8dc35","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"e3646f1e969299c351c53532bf2a7050fd9e5d6f6c7c535ed580c25c5aa9f635"},"suggested_fix":"Either state the behaviour (a revoke stops further snapshots; the error callback runs when the view next reconnects) in both .d.ts copies, or have the shell learn of the revoke (for instance the daemon sending refused on the reader topic when a grant is deleted) and end the listener then.","summary":"The contract says a revoked grant ends a live db.artifact(id) listener with not_granted, but the listener only stops receiving: it ends at the stream's next ready or resync","tags":["review","W3","contract","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.893293Z","id":"1dc0eff151c99c00b7fa52e00d09f58b62cb3386f1e617e607ef594611004f1c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:215522bf","summary":"The DbCrossReadErrorCode doc now says a revoke stops live updates at once and the listener hears not_granted at its next refresh (a stream reconnect), and later get() rejects not_granted; apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/clax-extensions.d.ts synced (scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check passes)","supersedes":"dbb3f8a4af960c891c35f4acbff42152dafadbc6ce81d1822beda2f284a3d1df","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:03:24.715287Z","id":"2af0a7936119a28201791a295485145c6ca4452d0b3de2f5f4a3bddaea90ae90","body":{"detail":"homeHandler (web/shell/src/caps/home.ts) gates every non-read call on frameGesture(), whose first rule is navigator.userActivation.isActive (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:548-553). Browsers grant activation for touch on touchend/pointerup, not while a finger rests, as web/bridge/src/long-press.ts:1-12 notes for comment-mode picks; contextmenu is not an activation-triggering event. The plan's Task 2 step 1 has home.js call menu on a 500 ms pointer hold or contextmenu, which would succeed only inside the activation window of an earlier tap. Opening apps automatically after a make is unaffected: MakeService.onMade hands the app over in Flutter (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart:287).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":294},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"905e3329d5a34f08fa5e493891f89869fcdd11f0d1b80d01f604db13866049e6"},"suggested_fix":"Either state in this comment that menu must be called from the hold's release (pointerup/touchend), and have home.js open the menu on release; or treat menu as a read (it only shows Flutter's sheet, whose items need a tap in Flutter).","summary":"home.menu needs a gesture, but a touch hold has no user activation until the finger lifts, so a menu opened from a 500 ms hold timer rejects no_gesture on a phone","tags":["review","gesture","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:03:24.715327Z","id":"0658e1289748854370d18e9f46e704b422fe5b229cd8ae5ad822839bc6910285","body":{"detail":"AppScreen forwards each HomeHost event while its route is covered (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:530-537), and HomeHost dedupes only unchanged values (_told in apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart). A covered page hears each change in turn, the last being the latest state; what is guaranteed is that the latest value arrives.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":367},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"423aa6951ee6aea3e846c890ce1ea699948447d52f0bd89802a3ebd010e37a14"},"suggested_fix":"Say: each change is delivered, and the last one carries the topic's latest value.","summary":"on()'s note that a covered page hears only the latest value overstates it: the app pushes every change to the covered page","tags":["review","docs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
